From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:29:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: defer the probe until the EEPROM NVMEM cell is
 ready

mt76_eeprom_init() turned every error from the device tree lookup into
"no EEPROM in the device tree", including -EPROBE_DEFER from an
"eeprom" NVMEM cell whose provider hasn't probed yet. The driver then
went on with efuse or the default EEPROM file, i.e. without the board's
calibration data, instead of trying again once the cell is there. The
GL-MT6000 takes its EEPROM from such a cell, on an eMMC partition.

Pass -EPROBE_DEFER on; all callers already return negative values, and
mt7915 now cleans up after a failed init. Un-skip
mt76_eeprom_test_init_nvmem_defer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 eeprom.c            | 9 ++++++++-
 tests/eeprom-test.c | 2 --
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/eeprom.c b/eeprom.c
index 913fccd0..6503cc24 100644
--- a/eeprom.c
+++ b/eeprom.c
@@ -549,12 +549,19 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt76_get_rate_power_limits);
 int
 mt76_eeprom_init(struct mt76_dev *dev, int len)
 {
+	int ret;
+
 	dev->eeprom.size = len;
 	dev->eeprom.data = devm_kzalloc(dev->dev, len, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!dev->eeprom.data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	return !mt76_get_of_eeprom(dev, dev->eeprom.data, len);
+	ret = mt76_get_of_eeprom(dev, dev->eeprom.data, len);
+	/* the EEPROM is there, its NVMEM provider just hasn't probed yet */
+	if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+		return ret;
+
+	return !ret;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt76_eeprom_init);
 
diff --git a/tests/eeprom-test.c b/tests/eeprom-test.c
index e3512290..1ae703f3 100644
--- a/tests/eeprom-test.c
+++ b/tests/eeprom-test.c
@@ -351,8 +351,6 @@ static void mt76_eeprom_test_init_nvmem_defer(struct kunit *test)
 	struct mt76_dev *dev;
 	struct device_node *np, *live;
 
-	kunit_skip(test, "driver bug: mt76_eeprom_init() returns 0 (no EEPROM in DT, use efuse/default) when the eeprom NVMEM cell returns -EPROBE_DEFER");
-
 	dev = mt76_eeprom_test_dev(test);
 	np = mt76_eeprom_test_of(test, dev);
 	live = mt76_eeprom_test_live(test);
